      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The most effective approach is a balanced curriculum that acknowledges both national achievements and historical challenges to provide a comprehensive understanding of reality. Relying exclusively on triumphs can foster blind patriotism, while focusing solely on injustices may lead to cynicism without context. Integrating both perspectives helps students develop critical thinking skills and empathy by seeing history as a complex, evolving narrative rather than a simplified story of unity or conflict.",
      "source": "target",
